WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.602
-Chloe Bailey,
you look gorgeous.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.904
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.973
You've been on my show
a bunch of times performing.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.207
-Yeah.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.742
-But now I finally
get a chance to talk to you.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.444
-I'm so happy to do this.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.112
You always have, like,
the best energy

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.513
and make me feel
so warm inside,

00:00:14.513 --> 00:00:16.282
so I'm happy we get
to do this again.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.650
Thank you.
-Oh, good. I'm loving this.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.919
Alright, perfect.
First of all, "That's My Jam."

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.955
You crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.590
-Wait till you see Chloe Bailey.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.425
You crushed it on the show.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.993
I had the best time.
-Did you have fun?

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.128
-Yes. Halle and I,
we were so excited.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.630
And I think what made it
more exciting

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.730
is how we were
on separate teams,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.132
how you guys split us up.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.166
-Did you think you were going
to be on the same team?

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.436
-Yes, and if we were
on the same team,

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:39.338
I think we would have won.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.840
-We would have beat out
anybody's butt.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.941
-No, yeah, because you were --

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.511
[ Applause ]

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.147
-But you are,
you're a professional.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.514
I mean,
you're professional singers.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:49.982
You can really sing.
-Thanks.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.951
-Yeah, I mean...
-Sometimes.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.119
-There's a mix
that we do on the show

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:56.456
that is so good
of breakup songs,

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.957
but you guys got
to wait to see that.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.260
It's really, really good.
-Oh, I can't wait.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.795
-Is it tough competing
against your sister?

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.364
-With competitive
games like that?

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.466
No, because I'm so competitive
and I love to win,

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:08.734
and she loves to win as well,

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.069
so it just makes it
more exciting.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.271
-I wanted to show a clip,
just because

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.641
you made your sister
kind of get sprayed

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.442
just because you were
such a good singer.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:17.643
Look at you laughing.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.312
It made you that happy
to spray your sister?

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.180
-No, because we were
so nervous about our hair

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.615
and makeup, we were like,
"Ahh, no."

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.584
-And it happened to her?
-Yeah.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.686
-Here's a taste of
next Monday's episode of

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.686
"That's My Jam," take a look.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:29.589 line:0%
-♪ I don't want no scrub ♪

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:33.092 line:0%
♪ A scrub is a guy
that can't get no love from me ♪

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.161 line:0%
♪ Hangin out the passenger side
of his best friend's ride ♪

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:38.498 line:0%
♪ Trying to holler at me ♪

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.599 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.935 line:0%
-[ Screams ]

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.505 line:0%
-It keeps going!

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.775
-I'm so sorry.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.410
Yeah,
I knew as soon as you started.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.013
I knew when it started,
I'm like, "Oh."

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.382
-Oh, man, that was so fun.
That was so fun.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.583
-Was there a moment
that you realized

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.419
that you knew
you wanted to be a singer?

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:03.389
-When I was 2 or 3, my aunt,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.592
she always tells
the story how I was singing

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.927
"Fallin'" by Alicia Keys
in my car seat.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.429
And she goes to my parents
and she's like,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.997
"Did you know she can sing?"

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.533
So I feel like I've been doing
music ever since I could talk.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.967
-Wow.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.904
-That was the jam, Alicia Keys.
Who else influenced you?

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.206
-Beyonce, Missy Elliott,
Alicia Keys.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.341
And the crazy thing is,
that was the first concert

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:25.979
I went to in Atlanta, and I had
my little Dangerously in Love

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.813
binoculars from
the nosebleed seats.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:30.049
And I was looking down
and five-year-old Chloe

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.218
was like, "You know what?
I'm gonna do that one day."

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.353
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.653
-Wow.
-That's when I knew.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:36.489
-Yeah, I love that
you just knew that right there.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.257
And weirdly, you ended up --

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.692
well, you worked
with Beyonce, right?

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.227
-Yeah. Yeah.
-On a movie.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.928
-Isn't that crazy?
"Fighting Temptations."

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:44.964
-"The Fighting Temptations."
I love that movie.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.000
Here's a picture of
you and Beyonce,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.269
you as a --
[ Crowd awws ]

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.505
How was that experience?

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.006
-I remember this exact moment.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.674
One, I just was in love
with my outfit

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:57.676
and my little flip-flop wedges.

00:02:57.676 --> 00:03:00.046
And when I saw that we were
in the same color,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.513
I got really excited
and I was like,

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:03.215
"Can I take a picture, please?"

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.550
And she was so nice to me.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.818
And even at the wrap party,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.687
she'd hold me
and we danced the night away.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.588
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:10.890
-She is really, unbelievably...

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.725
-She's...
-She should be where she is.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.993
-Yeah.
-'Cause she's so nice

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.828
to everybody.
-She's incredibly amazing.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.063
And even at the premiere,
it was really funny.

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:20.065
Halle and I, we were crawling
under people's legs

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.300
just to get to her.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.235
And sis's hair
got caught in her dress.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.604
She had, like, a sequins dress.
Isn't that funny?

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:27.473
-She got her hair caught
and Beyonce's dress?

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.343
-Mm-hmm.
-Was she cool with it?

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.644
-Yeah, she was fine with it.
She was so graceful.

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:34.313
And Halle and I were excited,
and I feel like

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.649
that was the moment
my love really began for her,

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.384
because she was so kind
to little Chloe.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.787
-Well, fast forward 20 years,
little Chloe.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.122
Now you are amazing,

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.424
and you're signed
to Beyonce's record label,

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:50.429
and you just released
your debut solo album.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:51.798
Yes.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.100
-Chloe, it's called "In Pieces."

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.501
-Yes, it is.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.637
-And you designed this album
cover yourself, by the way.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.872
I actually like
this part right here.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.974
-Yeah.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.810
I saw this photo
of a porcelain doll,

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.913
and she was holding, like,
a bloodied heart and like,

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.448
she ripped it out of her chest,
and she was like,

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:11.950
in kind of like
a Victorian outfit like this.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.019
-Yeah.
-And I was so inspired.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.754
And just off of that photo,

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.956
I created the song
that's on the album now,

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.958
"Heart on My Sleeve,"
like three years ago,

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.060
because I wanted to be
so open and vulnerable

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.695
about my feelings
and my emotions

00:04:23.695 --> 00:04:26.966
and how loving and giving
and naive I could be at times,

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.668
and it would stab me in the back
and the butt every time.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:30.903
So I was like, you know what?

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.906
I'm going to make an album
all about heartbreak

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.274
and feeling like
you're not good enough.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.876
And even though you might
seem perfect on the outside,

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:40.346
like the porcelain doll,
when you come extra close,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.247
you'll see all the little cracks
from breaking

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.150
and gluing yourself
back together again.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.585
Yeah, so that's why I called it
"In Pieces," for sure.

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:48.054
-I love that.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:50.989
That's fantastic.
Congratulations. Well done.

00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:52.959
It's a great record.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.560
That means a lot,
coming from you.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.562
-And also, I want to
tell about your movie,

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.964
"Praise This."
-Yes.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:00.365
It's on streaming,
on Peacock as of today.

00:05:00.365 --> 00:05:01.534
It's brand new.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.035
Can you tell everyone
what the movie is about?

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:06.204
-Yes, so Praise This,"
I play a girl named Sam.

00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:08.775
She's a struggling musician
and she's willing to do

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:11.143
whatever to get her career
off the ground,

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:13.545
like, she gets herself
into some trouble.

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:16.816
And she's quite a B-word.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:20.786
But she goes with
her family in Atlanta

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.988
and she somehow
gets mixed up with

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:24.323
the gospel praise team crowd.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.793
-Yeah. Do you like
playing this character?

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.694
-I do. Because you know why?

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.430
-Can I guess why?
-Yeah.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.167
-Because I think
you're so not a B-word,

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:37.403
so when you get to play one,

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.905
it's like, "Let's go."
-"Let's go."

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.407
-Am I right?
-No, it was amazing,

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:44.209
because all of my pent-up
emotion and like,

00:05:44.209 --> 00:05:46.412
comebacks that I wanted
to say back to people

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.080
that I thought
about the next day

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.683
but never had the chance to say,
I got to say it as Sam.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.152
-Yeah, you got to say it as Sam.
-Let's go!

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.188
-And you get to sing.
-And I got to sing.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.056
-You get to sing. You can act.

00:05:58.056 --> 00:06:00.559
You got it all, pal.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:03.863
Here's Chloe Bailey
in "Praise This." Take a look.

